            <div xml:id="d676">

                <pb facs="0707" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760F.62/1309: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-29T17:00:00+01:00">September 29, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 29—1:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>274. My telegram No. 268, September 28, 5 p.m. Although I was not afforded an
                    opportunity to present the President’s message to the Duce until nearly 4 p.m.
                    yesterday it may nevertheless be of interest to point out that the Foreign
                    Office and very probably the Duce himself knew before 10 a.m. that such a
                    message had arrived, whereas Lord Perth did not make his first call on Ciano
                    until 10:30.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
